From 783b397d81730e72da60e4cda3277db618a6aea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giorgos Sarigiannidis <contact@gsarigiannidis.gr>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:24:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Add the Conflicts tab (--conflicts DIR)

A Conflicts tab for Meld: every conflicted file of a git
repository, grouped Unresolved, Auto-resolved and Resolved, with Yours
and Theirs status and an Accept button per side (that side's version
staged, or its deletion for a side that deleted the file).

Double-click or Merge opens a file in the anchored merge view, in a tab
of its own, whose bottom button becomes Save and back to list; saving
with nothing unresolved stages the file. Resolve all simple conflicts
merges every file without a real conflict, word by word, keeping each
file's line breaks, and leaves it unstaged under Auto-resolved for
review; Accept and finish stages those and closes Meld. Deleted-on-one-
side and binary files offer only Accept.

Column titles and the header come from MELD_CONFLICTS_YOURS, _THEIRS and
_HEADER, set by the wrapper that knows the branch names.
